          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes and photographs two orange lights in the sky, static and appearing very distant. The objects disappear after a few minutes, however. The observation of two orange lights in the sky for a few minutes, on a weekend night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The lights, observed towards the southeast, seemed stationary, which is consistent with the near-zero wind, variable, recorded in Albi: weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
